  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs a user, I want the app to address me the same way everywhere, so that it reads as one app.\n\n### Rule\n\n\"Create a list of common terms, and reference that list to keep your language consistent. Consistent language, along with a voice that reflects your app's values, helps everything feel more cohesive.\" — [HIG › Writing](https://developer.apple.com/design/human-interface-guidelines/writing) (Determine your app's voice; page updated 2025-12-16).\n\n### What the app does (dev-swift @ `7a61018f`)\n\n- `App/SwiftHFR/Settings/PseudoListEditorView.swift:18`: « Connecte-toi pour gérer la liste noire de ton compte. »\n- `App/SwiftHFR/Reader/Search/TopicSearchModel.swift:111`: « Connecte-toi pour rechercher dans ce sujet. »\n\nThe same situation elsewhere says « Connectez-vous pour rechercher dans un sujet. » (`Reader/TopicReaderView.swift:132`) and « Connectez-vous pour utiliser le stockage MP. » (`MPStorage/MPStorageSettingsSection.swift:17`). These are the only two « tu » strings found.\n\n### Legacy at `87fe0d1c`\n\nConsistently « vous » (`HFRswift/Swift/AppSettingsView.swift:260`, `Favorites.swift:669`, `MPListView.swift:583`); `git grep -n \"Connecte-toi\" 87fe0d1c -- HFRswift` is empty.\n\n### Class\n\n**(a) defect** (parity), trivial.\n\n### Proposed fix and check\n\n- Both strings in the « vous » form.\n- Check: `grep -rn \"Connecte-toi\" App/SwiftHFR` returns nothing.\n\nRelated: #824 (logged-out prompts: same messages, another topic).\n\nFound by #866 (cloud/r866-fable, Fable 5.2)",
